 36MG    C(40AL,36MGG),1H(40AL,36MG)   2019CR02                  ENSDF    202106
 36MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=21-MAY-2021$                    
 36MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=12-MAR-2019$                    
 36MG c  1p1n-knockout reaction.                                                
 36MG c  2019Cr02: {+40}Al secondary beam was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X),    
 36MG2c  E=345 MeV/nucleon primary reaction at RIBF-RIKEN facility.             
 36MG3c  Rotating {+9}Be target was 2.8 mg/cm{+2} thick. Projectile-like        
 36MG4c  secondary fragments were selected using B|r-|DE-B|r method through the 
 36MG5c  BigRIPS fragment separator. Cocktail beam (consisting of {+41}Al and   
 36MG6c  {+40}Al) was incident on 3.82 g/cm{+2} thick polyethylene              
 36MG7c  ((C{-2}H{-4}){-n}) target placed at the focal point of the ZeroDegree  
 36MG8c  spectrometer (ZDS). Outgoing particles were identified in A/Q and Z    
 36MG9c  through event-by-event analysis by the B|r-|DE-tof method using the    
 36MGAc  ZDS spectrometer, and |g rays were detected using DALI2 array of 186   
 36MGBc  NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g rays in coincidence with      
 36MGCc  incoming {+40}Al beam particles and {+36}Mg outgoing particles.        
 36MGDc  Deduced level and J|p in {+36}Mg. Comparison with shell-model          
 36MGEc  calculations.                                                          
